the court condemns you to life  imprisonment that verdict was handed by  a court in dakar in 2016  after a year of trial for alleged crimes  against humanity  a graduate in political science from a  french university hussein habre was the  commander of a rebel group in northern  chad when he deposed gokoniwadai to take  over as president in 1982.  during his eight years in power he ruled  chad with an iron fist and was accused  of ordering the killings of his  political opponents an estimated 40 000  people died at the hands of his security  forces a human rights lawyer defending  the victims said habre was a pitiless  dictator who slaughtered his own people  burned down entire villages sent women  to serve as sex slaves for his soldiers  critics say during the time he committed  those atrocities he was enjoying close  ties with and support from both france  and the united states  abre was at war with america's arch  enemy in north africa at the time libyan  leader ammar qaddafi  president ronald reagan received habre  in the white house in 1987. president  habry emphasized that his government  is committed to building a better life  for the chadian people  habrev fled to senegal following a coup  in 1990 an arrest warrant was issued  against him in 2005 after some of his  victims filed a suit against him senegal  was reluctant to try him but habre was  arrested in 2013  after an intervention by the african  union he strongly objected to his trial  and the life term awarded to him  he was the first former african head of  state to be tried and convicted on  african soil through an african-led  legal process senegalese prison  officials say heisei and habre died on  tuesday after a cov19 infection
 

